            <p>Lateral Knee Fracture With Lipohemarthrosis, Radiograph. A lateral knee fracture with lipohemarthrosis indicates the presence of an intraarticular fracture, where fat and blood from bone marrow enter the joint space, producing a characteristic fat&#x02013;fluid level on imaging that confirms communication between the fracture and the joint capsule. Contributed by S Dulebohn, MD</p>
